CM ============================================================
CM  TM-SC-NEC-012: Screwdriver Antenna — 2m Band
CM  Whip element 0.488m, thin radius 0.0015m, NO loading coil
CM  Frequency: 144.000–148.000 MHz (9 points, 0.500 MHz step)
CM
CM  Configuration: dedicated 2m whip element (VHF stub).
CM  0.488m = 0.234 lambda at 146 MHz (nominal QW = 0.513m at 146 MHz)
CM  Slightly short; adjust physical length for true resonance.
CM  Radius reduced to 0.0015m — typical thin VHF whip construction.
CM  No loading coil; direct feed at base.
CM
CM  Whip: 0.488m, radius 0.0015m, 10 segments
CM  Radials: 4 x 0.488m at z=0.005m, 90 deg spacing, radius 0.0015m
CM  Ground: real (Sommerfeld-Norton), eps=13, sigma=0.005
CM  Feed: 1V voltage source at GW1, seg 1
CM  No LD card (no loading coil on 2m)
CM
CM  Tuning note: at 146 MHz, ground-wave effects are minimal.
CM  Azimuth pattern is omnidirectional as expected for vertical monopole.
CM  Elevation pattern peaks near 15-20 deg above horizon.
CM  Vehicle body coupling is significant at 2m — results here
CM  represent idealized 4-radial ground plane, not vehicle-mounted.
CM  For vehicle-mount modeling, a large conducting plate (hood/roof)
CM  should replace the radial system; this model is a baseline reference.
CM  FR sweep: 144.000-148.000 MHz (2m band, US).
